NNAAMMEE
     ppsstt — device driver for Promise Supertrak SX6000

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following line in your
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee ppsstt

     Alternatively, to load the driver as a module at boot time, place the
     following line in loader.conf(5):

           pst_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     This driver is for the Promise Supertrak SX6000 ATA hardware RAID con‐
     troller.  It supports (in hardware) RAID levels 0, 1, 0+1, 3, 5 and JBOD
     on up to 6 ATA disk drives, including automatic rebuild and hotswap, and
     supports signalling disk status on LEDs on Promise Superswap disk enclo‐
     sures.  The Supertrak line of controllers does not support non-disk de‐
     vices.

HHAARRDDWWAARREE
     The ppsstt driver supports the Promise Supertrak SX6000 ATA hardware RAID
     controller.

NNOOTTEESS
     The ppsstt driver does not support manipulating the RAID from the OS, RAIDs
     need to be set up from the onboard BIOS.  However, hot swap, hot spare,
     and automatic rebuilds are supported without a reboot.

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The ppsstt driver first appeared in FreeBSD 4.7.

